  "problem": "Classify the critical points using the second partial derivatives test.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$ are local maximum since $\\,H(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$0\\,\\,$ and $\\,\\,\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{x}^{2}}(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$0$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(0,0)$ is a saddle point since $\\,\\,H(0,0)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$0$",
  "worked_solution": "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nIn part 4, we found the critical points $(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,0).$ Their corresponding Hessian determinants and the second partial derivatives at these points were computed in part 6.\n\nWith that in mind, let's classify our critical points:\n\n- $(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$ are local maximum of $f$ since $H(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})=2\\,160>0$ and $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{x}^{2}}(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})=-54<0.$\n\n- $(0,0)$ is a saddle point since $H(0,0)=-80<0.$",
